  PaginateExceptionFilter.OnException: the method was rewritten so the two pipelines enrich a
  ProblemDetails exactly once each, and its nullable context moved with it. The behaviour is the
  change; the attribute is a side effect.

  WithPagination(RouteHandlerBuilder): nothing about this overload changed. Adding a second one for a
  route group moved the class's nullable-context encoding, so the existing member reads as having lost
  NullableContextAttribute(1). No signature and no nullability actually differs.

  Both are visible only because the ApiCompat attribute rule is now on — nullable context lives in
  metadata the signature comparison does not read, so either would have shipped silently before.

  Delete this file when PackageValidationBaselineVersion moves past 10.0.3: the entries exist only
  against that baseline, and a stale suppression hides the next accidental break behind it.
-->
